{title: Salt and Light}
{subtitle: Matthew 5:13–16}
{key: C}
{tempo: 115}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [F] [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]A little pinch of salt makes the [F]dinner taste so [G]good
[C]A little candle shines in the dark [F]the way it [G]should
[F]Jesus looked at all his friends [C]sitting on the [Am]hill
And [Dm]he told them who they are and [G]he tells us still
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are [C]the salt of the earth
You are [G]the light of the world
A [Am]city set on a hill can[F]not be [G]hidden
[C]Shine, shine, [G]shine
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]No one lights a lamp and puts [F]it under [G]a basket
[Am]They set it on [C]a stand
And it [F]gives light to every[G]one in the house
[F]So hold your little light [C]up high in [Am]your hand
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[F]Help your friend, [C/E]share your bread
[Dm]Say a kind word, like [C]Jesus said
[F]Let your light shine be[C/E]fore others
So [Dm]that they may see your good [G]works
And glorify your Father in heaven
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
You are the [C]light of the world
[G]Shine, shine, [C]shine
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
